{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0518-building-an-ncaa-mens-basketball-predictive.md", "equation": "Simulations (Table 3): if S₂ were the true probabilities, S₂'s median rank = 14, P(win) = 11.65%, P(top-10) = 44.47%; if S₁ true, S₁ P(win) = 15.57%, P(top-10) = 48.79%. Vs random-winner baseline (1/433 ≈ 0.23%), skill multiplies win odds ~50–60×. Under median-of-top-10 as truth, P(win) ≈ 2% for both; under all-coin-flip, neither ever won. 332–348 unique winners of 433 across simulations (~20% of entries never winnable).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
