{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0542-bradleyterry-rankings-for-recommender-systems-across.md", "equation": "Estimation (three variants, compared):** (1) classic Zermelo MLE iteration p′_i = Σ_j W_{ij} / Σ_j (W_{ij}+W_{ji})/(p_i+p_j), normalized by geometric mean; (2) Bayesian BT: W_{ij} ∼ Binomial(N_{ij}, e^{β_i}/(e^{β_i}+e^{β_j})), β_i ∼ Normal(0, σ̄), σ̄ ∼ LogNormal(0, 0.5), Metropolis-Hastings → posterior samples give CIs on weights and P(i≻j); (3) rank centrality (spectral): random walk on comparison graph, θ*_i from stationary distribution. On the complete win matrix all three converge to identical weights; the Bayesian variant is used for its confidence intervals.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0542-bradleyterry-rankings-for-recommender-systems-across.md", "equation": "Covariate-adjusted BT.** P(i ≻ j | x) = σ(β_{i0} − β_{j0} + ⟨x,β_i⟩ − ⟨x,β_j⟩); n(d+1) parameters; identifiability Σ_i β_{ij} = 0 ∀j. Fitted by penalized MLE: ℓ(B) − L(B) with fusion penalty L(B) = λ_0 Σ_{i<j} √((β_{i0}−β_{j0})²+ε) + λ_1 Σ_k Σ_{i<j} √((β_{ik}−β_{jk})²+ε) (shrinks overall strengths together and covariate effects together to avoid overfitting to the static global ranking); L-BFGS-B. Covariates: log-normalized numeric + binary categorical dataset characteristics. Predict ranking on a new dataset by sorting β_{i0} + ⟨x, β_i⟩. **BT trees** (psychotree R package): recursive partition of datasets by covariates (e.g., forced root split on sequentiality → number of users → interactions/user), leaf = BT ranking; zero-cost prediction by tree traversal.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0542-bradleyterry-rankings-for-recommender-systems-across.md", "equation": "BT: Pr(i ≻ j) = p_i/(p_i + p_j), Σ_i p_i = 1 or Π_i p_i = 1.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
