{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0543-rethinking-sales-lead-scoring-with-llmbased.md", "equation": "1. **Game-importance-weighted team ratings via tiered-margin BT.** Port: define an NFL \"funnel\" hierarchy of game informativeness — e.g., Playoff games ≻ late-season games between contenders ≻ early-season games (mirroring P_global/P_key/P_soft with margins m=1.0/0.5/0.1 as starting values, then tune). For BT rating fits, weight pairwise comparisons with margin-aware targets P(i≻j | m) = σ(θ_i − θ_j − m) so that ratings separate more on high-information games — the same mechanism the paper uses to separate lock-in vs defeat leads. Data: nflverse 2015–2025 game results + playoff flags. Effort: ~2 days (win-matrix → margin-aware BT objective; compare to static BT on the §12 test).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0543-rethinking-sales-lead-scoring-with-llmbased.md", "equation": "Dataset:** nflverse 2018–2024 regular + postseason games; outcome = SU winner; tier assignment: playoff games (m=1.0 tier), weeks 12–17 non-playoff (m=0.5), weeks 1–11 (m=0.1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0544-regularization-in-paired-comparison-models-via.md", "equation": "General schema:** paired-comparison win counts y_ij (times i beats j), m_ij = y_ij + y_ji, probabilities p_ij = F(θ_i − θ_j) with F = logistic (BT) or Φ (TM).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0544-regularization-in-paired-comparison-models-via.md", "equation": "Linear paired-comparison model: p_ij = F(θ_i − θ_j), F(x) = 1−F(−x) (Eq. 1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9127}
